{{Codex|A high-capacity, high-damage enforcer, this weapon can switch between the high crit semi-automatic and full automatic firing modes.}}
The '''Stradavar''' is a {{Faction|Tenno}} assault rifle featuring the ability to switch between semi- and fully-automatic firing modes by using the [[Alternate Fire]].

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Impact}} and {{D|Puncture}} by a slight margin on its full-auto mode, and {{D|Puncture}} damage on its semi-auto mode.

{{Advantages|
*Full-auto mode has negligible [[recoil]].
*Semi-auto mode has high accuracy when aiming.
}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Semi-auto mode has the second-lowest damage of all semi-automatic rifles, after {{Weapon|Tiberon Prime}}.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Stradavar Prime}}

==Acquisition==
The Stradavar's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]]. If [[Mastery Rank|unmastered]], it can also be obtained via the daily login system as a random reward.
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}
This weapon can be sold for {{cc|7,500}}.

==Trivia==
*The Stradavar's design bears a strong resemblance to several machine guns utilizing a [[wikipedia:Magazine (firearms)#Pan/Disc|drum-pan magazine]], such as the British-built [[wikipedia:Vickers K machine gun|Vickers K]] and [[wikipedia:Lewis gun|Lewis Gun]], the US-built [[wikipedia:American-180|American-180]], and the Russian-built [[wikipedia:Degtyaryov machine gun|DP-28]].
**The Stradavar further resembles the Lewis gun without its barrel shroud, or the [[wikipedia:Type_92_machine_gun|Type 92 machine gun]].
*The Stradavar's name seems to be based on ''[[wikipedia:Stradivarius|Stradivarius]]'', which is a name given to highly regarded string instruments that were created by the Italian Stradivari family. It's also a reference to pre-WW2 American Mafia culture when it was romanticized that gangsters would carry submachine guns in violin cases.
*The Stradavar's last fourteen shots sound slightly different to indicate low ammunition in the magazine.
**Shots from the single fire mode are also a bit louder.
*Prior to the Specters of the Rail update, Stradavar had identical damage on both firing modes and a lower status chance.
*With the addition of [[Update 21]] the Stradavar became the first weapon with increased accuracy when fired at the hip and ''reduced'' accuracy when firing while zooming (in full auto).

