{{Codex|An energy projectile bursts forth from the Steflos as it rushes towards enemies. The projectile's duration increases when it hits an enemy. When Citrine fires the Steflos, its projectile speed increases.}}

'''Steflos''' is {{WF|Citrine}}'s [[Signature Weapon|signature]] shotgun that fires large {{D|Heat}} energy projectiles. These projectiles are initially short-ranged, but grow in size and last longer as it passes through enemies. In Citrine's hands, the weapon gains increased [[Projectile Speed]].

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Heat}} damage.
*Projectiles have lifespan of '''0.6''' seconds.
*Projectiles grow in size and last longer as it hits enemies.
**Each enemy hit increases projectile lifespan by '''50%''', up to a max projectile lifespan of '''10''' seconds.

{{Advantages|class=Shotgun|
*Projectiles have a base thickness of ~2 meters.
*Innate [[Infinite Body Punch Through]].
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Shotgun|
*Has linear damage falloff from 100% to 3.125% from 8m to 16m target distance (distances are affected by [[Projectile Speed]]).
*Projectile has travel time.
*Limited base range of 12 meters (can be increased with [[Projectile Speed]] mods).
*Innate [[punch through]] does not apply to surfaces if hitting with the central portion of the projectile, requiring [[punch through]] mods.
}}
{{WeaponComparison|Steflos Prime}}

{{Acquisition|Steflos's blueprint and components can be obtained from [[Mirror Defense]] [[Tyana Pass]] on [[Mars]], whose access requires completion of [[Heart of Deimos]]; the blueprint comes from [[Rotation]] A, while the Barrel, Receiver, and Stock come from Rotation B.

Alternatively they can be purchased from [[Otak]] in the [[Necralisk]], [[Deimos]] with {{Resource|Belric Crystal Fragment}} and {{Resource|Rania Crystal Fragment}}, awarded from Mirror Defense in quantities of 5 (7 on [[The Steel Path]]) cycling between the two from collecting Citrine's Remnants, and in quantities of 10 (15 on The Steel Path) per rotation; each component requires 250 Belric and 150 Rania, while the blueprint requires 500 Belric and 300 Rania, totaling to 1,250 Belric and 750 Rania Crystal Fragments.

All components can be [[Trading|traded]] between players, but '''not''' the blueprint.}}

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*When wielded by {{WF|Citrine}}/{{WF|Citrine Prime}}, Steflos gains '''40%''' [[Projectile Speed]].
*Hitting enemies increases projectile lifespan by '''50%''' per enemy hit, up to a max projectile lifespan of '''10''' seconds.

== Known Bugs ==
* {{M|Galvanized Savvy}} is multiplicative to base damage sources on direct hits.

